WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.543
- Like it's a dream to win a championship,

00:00:01.543 --> 00:00:04.421
but it's a dream to have the ball in your hands when the buzzer goes off.

00:00:04.421 --> 00:00:05.422
I knew I was keeping it.

00:00:05.422 --> 00:00:06.673
Like, I wasn’t gonna throw it. 

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.591
Like, sometimes you see, like, people, like, throw it.

00:00:08.591 --> 00:00:09.759
- You see Kobe do that?

00:00:09.759 --> 00:00:11.094
- Yeah, throw it up and all that. 

00:00:11.094 --> 00:00:13.263
I'm like, "Nah, I'm keeping this. I don't care what happens.”

00:00:13.263 --> 00:00:22.147
♪♪♪

00:00:22.147 --> 00:00:23.857
[Master Tesfatsion:] So, who we got in the pool hall today?

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.692
Oh, we got Coach Kara Lawson. What’s up?

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:26.276
- [Kara Lawson:] [Laughing]

00:00:26.276 --> 00:00:27.777
- DMV’s finest. How you living?

00:00:27.777 --> 00:00:28.862
- Doing good. Great.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.321
- You're one of the nicest players in the DMV,

00:00:30.321 --> 00:00:31.614
but how nice are you on the pool table?

00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:33.199
-  Uh, I'm, I'm OK.

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:34.617
- [Laughing]

00:00:34.617 --> 00:00:36.870
- Needs work. Needs work. But we’ll try.
- Let's see what you can do.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.288
Let’s see what you can do on the break.

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:40.415
There we go.

00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:43.918
You spent the majority of your time in the WNBA

00:00:43.918 --> 00:00:45.962
 with the Sacramento Monarchs, but you were drafted by the Shock.

00:00:45.962 --> 00:00:46.629
- Yeah.

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:47.505
- What happened on draft night?

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:50.592
- Well, I get drafted. And it's exciting, obviously.

00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:53.636
My mom, my dad, excited about getting drafted.

00:00:53.636 --> 00:00:56.389
Bill Laimbeer was the coach of the Shock at the time.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.141
I get on the phone and Laimbeer's like, 

00:00:58.141 --> 00:01:00.477
"Yeah we're about to, we're gonna trade you."

00:01:00.477 --> 00:01:01.561
- [Laughing]

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:06.191
- Like, he didn't say like, "Congrats," or like, or like anything, you know? 

00:01:06.191 --> 00:01:10.320
He's just like, "Yeah, we're working on a 
trade so you're not gonna be here with us."

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:11.780
I'm like, “Welcome to the league.”

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:12.739
- [Laughing]

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.243
What do you remember, day one, when you got to Sacramento?

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.787
What do you recall from that moment?

00:01:18.787 --> 00:01:20.371
- I'd never been to Sacramento.

00:01:20.371 --> 00:01:22.957
So day one, I remember getting picked up at the airport 

00:01:22.957 --> 00:01:26.419
and people that have been in the league, NBA, WNBA,

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:28.838
like, there was nothing in Sacramento.

00:01:28.838 --> 00:01:29.672
- [Laughing]

00:01:29.672 --> 00:01:30.423
- Like, now it's different. 

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:33.760
Some people still might say there's nothing 
in Sacramento, but I love Sacramento.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:38.640
But then, it was like fields and, like, ARCO in the middle of nothing.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:39.390
- [Laughing]

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.017
- I was like, "Where am I?”

00:01:41.017 --> 00:01:41.893
- [Laughing]

00:01:41.893 --> 00:01:44.687
- I grew up in the DMV, went to school at Tennessee. 

00:01:44.687 --> 00:01:45.772
That was just an adjustment,

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.607
being out on your own for the first time now.

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:49.859
Hey.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.861
Strong shot.

00:01:52.237 --> 00:01:53.696
- That 2005 run,

00:01:53.696 --> 00:01:55.907
what was your favorite game that you recall from that moment?

00:01:55.907 --> 00:01:58.201
- Probably the close-out game. Probably Game 4.

00:01:58.201 --> 00:01:59.160
- How was ARCO that game?

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:00.411
- ARCO was crazy.

00:02:00.411 --> 00:02:01.621
 It was so loud.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:04.666
You know, they had never won a championship in the city before. 

00:02:04.666 --> 00:02:06.417
That was our last chance to do it there

00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:08.044
cuz we didn't have home-court in that series.

00:02:08.044 --> 00:02:10.255
We played 1 and 2 on the road. We played 3 and 4 at home. 

00:02:10.255 --> 00:02:13.758
So to close it out there at home in front of our fans was amazing.

00:02:15.385 --> 00:02:16.594
[Balls hitting, ball dropping into pocket]

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.222
- Well, with 0.4 seconds left.

00:02:19.222 --> 00:02:19.848
- Mhmm.

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:20.849
- Quick inbound to you.

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:21.391
- Yeah.

00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:22.725
- Clock goes triple zero.

00:02:22.725 --> 00:02:23.351
- Yeah.

00:02:23.768 --> 00:02:24.727
- How are you feeling?

00:02:24.727 --> 00:02:25.854
- I was feeling great.

00:02:25.854 --> 00:02:27.438
Like, it's a dream to win a championship,

00:02:27.438 --> 00:02:30.275
but it's a dream to have the ball in your hands when the buzzer goes off.

00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:32.318
And, so, I knew I was keeping it.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.237
Any picture you find of me that night,

00:02:34.237 --> 00:02:36.865
I got the ball in my hand cuz I didn't want anybody to take it.

00:02:36.865 --> 00:02:39.033
And then, I had everybody on the team sign it.

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.285
And I still have that ball.

00:02:40.285 --> 00:02:42.036
-  So you guys win the championship in 2005,

00:02:42.036 --> 00:02:45.707
and then you're the first pro women's team on a Wheaties box. 

00:02:46.082 --> 00:02:47.792
What does that mean? Do you still have that box too or no?

00:02:47.792 --> 00:02:49.919
- I still have it in a case at my mom's house.

00:02:49.919 --> 00:02:51.754
That cereal's gone, you know.

00:02:51.754 --> 00:02:52.255
- [Laughing]

00:02:52.255 --> 00:02:54.883
- Can't have that around for 15 years.

00:02:54.883 --> 00:02:55.717
- [Laughing]

00:02:55.717 --> 00:02:59.053
- But I still have the boxes, yeah. It was really cool.

00:02:59.053 --> 00:03:02.140
Growing up, being on a Wheaties box was like, I mean that was it.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:02.724
- Yeah.

00:03:04.225 --> 00:03:06.978
So your final year in Sacramento was in 2009,

00:03:06.978 --> 00:03:09.439
but it wasn't your choice. The team folded.

00:03:09.439 --> 00:03:10.982
What was that season like for you?

00:03:10.982 --> 00:03:12.942
- We did not know that that was coming.

00:03:12.942 --> 00:03:18.031
It was actually after the season. I got a
call from one of our front office people.

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:20.909
I was at my old college visiting Coach [Pat] Summitt

00:03:20.909 --> 00:03:23.369
Just got a phone call and they said that we’re done.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.288
And I was just in disbelief. 

00:03:25.288 --> 00:03:27.832
Not even emotional, just shocked.

00:03:27.832 --> 00:03:31.002
And so, you kind of lose a generation of players, fans

00:03:31.002 --> 00:03:34.797
and young people that could be inspired by,

00:03:34.797 --> 00:03:36.216
you know, women playing the game.

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:37.300
So that was hard.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.969
It was hard to transfer, but you have to do it quick.

00:03:39.969 --> 00:03:42.513
That is the nature of pro sports. You can get traded.

00:03:42.513 --> 00:03:46.184
So I just had to focus on what was next, but I still miss it.

00:03:46.184 --> 00:03:47.268
I still miss it out there.

00:03:47.268 --> 00:03:48.603
 - We talkin' WNBA expansion

00:03:48.603 --> 00:03:49.270
- [Lawson:] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.522
- The viewership is up, what, 30 percent already so far.

00:03:51.522 --> 00:03:51.898
- [Lawson:] Yeah.

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:54.317
- A lot more people are investing in the WNBA.

00:03:54.317 --> 00:03:56.319
What do you think the future’s like right now for women's basketball?

00:03:56.319 --> 00:03:59.364
- The athlete that you get now is as focused,

00:03:59.364 --> 00:04:01.783
as disciplined, as driven as before.

00:04:01.783 --> 00:04:05.954
They have unbelievable skill sets and size.

00:04:05.954 --> 00:04:06.287
- Mmm.

00:04:06.287 --> 00:04:08.873
- Like what some of the 6’5" players are able to do now

00:04:08.873 --> 00:04:10.917
is completely different than when I was in the league.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:11.751
- Well, what's different?

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.920
- The 6'5" players now can do everything.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.546
Or are allowed to do everything.

00:04:15.546 --> 00:04:18.091
I don't want to knock on the 6'5" players back then.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:20.927
But they weren't allowed to do what they're allowed to do now.

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.387
They were mostly post—

00:04:22.387 --> 00:04:23.805
-  Post people. Grabbing boards.

00:04:23.805 --> 00:04:24.681
- Yeah, things like that.

00:04:24.681 --> 00:04:25.473
- Rim protector.

00:04:25.473 --> 00:04:26.766
- And now, they do everything. 

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:28.893
Jonquel Jones is a beast. She does everything.

00:04:28.893 --> 00:04:31.938
She shoots like 45 percent from three. At 6'6".

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:33.815
Like, that's amazing, you know?

00:04:33.815 --> 00:04:35.692
Stewart and what she's able to do.

00:04:35.692 --> 00:04:38.778
There's this, the length and the athleticism

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:41.364
and the skill level is really impressive.

00:04:43.574 --> 00:04:44.117
Ahh!

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:45.285
- [Laughing]

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:50.415
- So Kara let’s see what you can do here in the Pop-A-Shot, all right?

00:04:50.415 --> 00:04:51.666
You’re gonna have 60 seconds.

00:04:51.666 --> 00:04:53.418
Gonna ask you some questions as you’re doing this.

00:04:53.418 --> 00:04:54.294
See how many you can make, all right?

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:54.794
- All right.

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:55.211
- Let’s get it.

00:04:55.211 --> 00:04:56.087
[Digital beeps from game sounding]

00:04:56.087 --> 00:04:58.131
- The one athlete dead or alive you’d wanna meet?

00:04:58.131 --> 00:05:00.591
- Oh. Wayne Gretzky.

00:05:00.675 --> 00:05:02.135
- Best city to visit on the road?

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.261
- D.C. Home.

00:05:03.553 --> 00:05:05.013
- Pregame snack meal routine.

00:05:05.013 --> 00:05:06.097
What’s your favorite pregame snack?

00:05:06.097 --> 00:05:07.890
- As a coach, not, I don’t eat a lot.

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:09.350
- [Laughing]

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:13.062
- As a player, probably like some chicken, rice.

00:05:13.062 --> 00:05:14.188
- Who're you listening to right now?

00:05:14.188 --> 00:05:15.064
- J. Cole.

00:05:15.064 --> 00:05:16.607
- 3-on-3 or 5-on-5?

00:05:16.607 --> 00:05:19.319
- Right now? In Tokyo? 3-on-3.

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:20.987
- Funniest teammate you ever had?

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:24.741
- Uh, probably a tie between Kalana Greene and Monique Currie.

00:05:24.741 --> 00:05:27.035
